*** Variables ***
# Variables for ue profile and traffic
${CallType}                 SA           # NSA or SA (for all UEs)
${Cell}                     1            # Target cell (must be index 1, 2, 3, 4, 5...)
${DLthroughput}             50           # DL throughput in Mbps
${ULthroughput}             10           # UL throughput in Mbps
${TrafficDuration}          10           # Traffic Duration  (0 means no traffic)

#Variables to Build UEs list and Setup WTS Lua
${gNbID}              2            # Value of the Target_gnb  
${CellID}             1            # Retrieved from NRCELL_ID_LIST items [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, None, None, None]
${ue_1_id}            1            # Applied only for KW SA Call of 1 UE
${ue_3_id}            3            # ue id 3

#Variables for TC 9158 Asymetric Band PRB Allocation
${csv_file_name_9158_K}     macro__dlStat.csv
${expected_MAX_PRB_9158_K}         98
${operator_compare_9158_K}         >=
${column_name_9158_K}            MAX PRB

# Now, the TestLine is configured during Suite Setup
# Custom Config File to be used during "Suite Setup"
${custom_config_file}       ${CURDIR}/../../../../../../../custom-config/POOLING/CB009158/CB009158_K/custom_config_9158_K.yaml

*** Keywords ***

Suite Setup 9158-K
    [Documentation]
    ...     Conditions:    it needs no conditions
    ...     Actions:       it performs the generic suite setup and backup the configurations files
    ...     Checks:        it checks nothing more than already done on lib.
    ...     Verdict:       suite setup is passed
    Setup.Suite Setup From Scratch
    ...                    keepAllUeDataInCfgFile=${True}
    ...                    automaticTeardown=${True}
    ...                    yamlPathname=${custom_config_file}
    Backup Files
    ${scf_suite_setup_backup}        OAM Get SCF File           file=SCF_Suite_Setup_Backup.xml
    Set Suite Variable               ${scf_suite_setup_backup}
    Dated Log                        SCF backup file = ${scf_suite_setup_backup}
		
TC 9158 Asymetric Band PRB Allocation
    [Documentation]         Vérification que le nombre de PRB alloués avec CB007933 activé ne dépasse jamais 98 Prbs en DL
        ...                 (inner guard period de 4 Prbs soit 102 Prbs
	...                 mais remis à RBG complet + 2 PRb = 98 Prbs max)

    [Arguments]            ${params}        ${Vendor_Param}
    Set Suite Variable     ${params}
    Init Sequence          ${params}
    Step                   Set RAD Params Of 1227
    Step                   Config1227.Vendor File Config With Specific Settings     argument=${Vendor_Param}
    Step                   Recommissioning
    Critical Step          Restart TL
    Step                   Multi Cells Setup SA 1227                   argument=${params.nbCell}
    Step                   Wait In Seconds
    Step                   SA Call With UE Id   argument=${ue_1_id}
    Step                   SA Call With UE Id   argument=${ue_3_id}
    Step                   Activate Sherpa On All Cells
    Step                   Wait In Seconds
    Step                   Stop Sherpa Collection
    Step                   Check PRB Allocation In Sherpa for CB009158-K

Check PRB Allocation In Sherpa for CB009158-K
    [Documentation]                  post-processing on macro_dlStat.csv to check that
    ...                                 - for DL, bw 20Mhz, the maxPRB will be <=98 (inner guard period not avaialble)
    Dated Log                        Analyse in sherpa traces : PRB allocation for DL grant
    Verify Max PRB In Sherpa      ${csv_file_name_9158_K}   ${column_name_9158_K}    ${expected_MAX_PRB_9158_K}   ${operator_compare_9158_K}
